city on the Mediterranean coast of southern Turkey.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/alaol"><span class="enc-name">Alaol</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alaol was a Bengali poet of the 17th century who lived at the court of Mrauk U in Arakan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alaouite-dynasty"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/alaouite-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alaouite dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Alaouite dynasty is the ruling house of Morocco, a sharifian family claiming descent from the Prophet Muhammad through his grandson Hasan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alaric-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/alaric-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alaric I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alaric I was a king of the Visigoths who led his people in conflicts with the Roman Empire in the late fourth and early fifth centuries.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alaric-ii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/alaric-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alaric II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alaric II was king of the Visigoths from 484 to 507, ruling much of Gaul and Hispania from Toulouse.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alasehir"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/alasehir.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alaşehir</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Alaşehir is a town in Manisa Province in western Turkey.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alash-party"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/alash-party.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alash (party)</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">Alash was a Kazakh national party founded in 1917 by intellectuals including Alikhan Bukeikhanov, Akhmet Baitursynov and Mirzhakip Dulatov, and named after the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alaska"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/alaska.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alaska</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Alaska is a large region in north-western North America.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/alatheus"><span class="enc-name">Alatheus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alatheus was a chieftain of the Greuthungi Goths who, with Saphrax, acted as guardian of the boy-king Vithericus after the Huns overran their people around 375.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alatri"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/alatri.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alatri</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Alatri, ancient Aletrium, is a hill town of the Hernici in southern Lazio, Italy, famous for its acropolis enclosed by massive polygonal walls of the pre-Roman period.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-al-kahar"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/alauddin-al-kahar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alauddin al-Kahar</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alauddin al-Kahar was sultan of Aceh from about 1537 to 1571 and made it a regional power.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-husain-shah"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclope